{
  "id": "COMPOUND:240 - DISEASE:886",
  "verbalization": "Dapsone appears to influence a molecular pathway that ultimately leads to the development of Double Outlet Right Ventricle. This is mediated through the immunoglobulin kappa variable 2D-29, which acts as a causal link between dapsone and a series of conditions, including Hyperopia, Epilepsy, and Kartagener Syndrome. These conditions, in turn, are linked to the same molecular target, suggesting a broader, interconnected network of effects. The evidence suggests that dapsone may modulate a biological process that results in the manifestation of Double Outlet Right Ventricle, though the exact mechanism remains partially obscured by the indirect pathways. The integration of these findings implies that dapsone could be a potential candidate for repurposing in the treatment of this condition, though further research is needed to clarify the precise role of the implicated pathways.",
